10. **Accelerator allocation.** Before claiming a GPU/accelerator for a job,
    check it isn't already in use by another job/agent; record which device
    index you're using in `.friday/active/harness/status.md` alongside the job. Tools that
    report device indices must agree with each other (e.g. `nvidia-smi`
    ordering vs. the framework's own numbering) — verify this once and note
    the mapping in `.friday/active/harness/rules/gpu.md` if they don't. **Trigger:** before
    launching any job that claims accelerator hardware →
    `.friday/active/harness/rules/gpu.md`.
<!-- SECTION:accel_present:end -->

11. **Fail-loud numerical guards.** A skip-bad-batch guard must also detect
    permanent collapse and abort loudly; "no valid batches" resolves to a
    FAILURE sentinel, never a success-looking zero. Monitors key on the
    sentinel/static-metric, not just the literal string `nan`. **Trigger:**
    writing a training guard or arming a health monitor →
    `.friday/active/harness/rules/monitoring.md`.

12. **Recording finished work.** Finished work leaves a durable record as a
    version-control commit, attributed to the role that did it, and a task
    is not done until that record's reference is pasted next to it.
    Never leave two agents' changes mingled in one unrecorded blob.
    **Trigger:** recording completed work, or judging whether work is
    done → `.friday/active/harness/rules/version_control.md`.

13. **External queue sync (opt-in).** Applies only when the project opts in
    by configuring a tracker (`TRACKER_KIND` != `none`; this project:
    `[SET AT SETUP: TRACKER_KIND]`; detail in `rules/task_tracking.md`). Then every directive gets
    one issue: the Controller opens it **when the user approves the
    directive** (not at proposal, so rejected proposals leave no issues),
    and the Reviewer closes it at close-out, same pass in both cases.
    Missing credentials **block** that step — no silent skip. **Trigger:**
    approving or closing a directive → `rules/task_tracking.md`.

