15. **Detached background launches.** Every long-running background job
    (training, multi-hour eval, monitor) is launched fully detached from its
    parent shell/terminal session, never a bare `cmd &` inside an
    interactive terminal — a killed/crashed terminal session can send SIGHUP
    (or, in a cgroup-managed environment like tmux-under-systemd, a
    cgroup-wide kill) to the whole process group and silently kill every
    un-detached child with it, leaving no traceback, no OOM signature, and
    no watchdog alert. **Trigger:** any `long_job ... &`-style launch →
    `.friday/active/harness/rules/environment.md` §Detached launches.

16. **Document budgets & concision.** Applies to directives tagged `[doc]`
    (a prose deliverable — theory, report, memo) and to Architect specs.
    Short working notes (READMEs, board summaries, a directive's Log) are
    exempt. Every `[doc]` deliverable carries a
    page budget stated in its directive's `Verify:` block, and **over budget
    is a defect with the same force as a broken citation**, not a stylistic
    note. No prose deliverable closes without an Editor subtractive pass
    (reported as `cut X lines / Y pages, math unchanged`) and a cold-reader
    check by a context-free utility spawn (dispatched by the Controller). Assumption tables cap at 8 rows;
    every core concept gets a figure. Exists because, in the project this
    rule originated in, a technically flawless long-form document shipped
    that its own reader could not learn from — every gate measured
    correctness, none measured length, and review was structurally
    additive. **Trigger:** working, planning or reviewing a
    `[doc]` directive, or writing a spec →
    `.friday/active/harness/rules/document_budgets.md`.
17. **Context hygiene.** Cost scales with context × turns: grep then read
    ranges, filter command output, never Read images/transcripts, one Step
    per worker session. **Trigger:** session start for any role that reads
    files or runs commands → `.friday/active/harness/rules/context_hygiene.md`.
18. **Long runs go to a Runner.** A command expected to take > ~4 min
    (full test suites, release or Docker/firmware builds, benches, hardware
    runs, training, sweeps) is never launch-and-waited by a big-context
    worker: an idle wait past the ~5-min prompt-cache lifetime re-writes its
    whole context. The worker logs a `Run request` and ends; a light-tier
    Runner launches, monitors and summarizes; a fresh worker acts on a
    failure. Any unavoidable wait stays ≤ ~4 min per turn. **Trigger:** any
    build, test suite, bench or run you expect to exceed ~4 min →
    `.friday/active/harness/rules/monitoring.md` §Long runs.

## Execution

Anything that runs code follows `.friday/active/harness/rules/environment.md` (environment
setup, launch pattern, key commands). Anyone launching/monitoring jobs
follows `.friday/active/harness/rules/monitoring.md`. Roles that never execute (e.g.
Author) skip both.
